      <main id="content" role="main">
        <div class="content-pages-show-basic-wide">
  <div class="row">
  <div class="col-12 col-lg-9 mx-auto">

    



<p> </p>
<div class="row mb-5">
  <div class="col-12">
    <p class="lead" style="color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.7;">This new service allows residents to send a text message to 911 in situations where calling may not be possible or safe. This initiative is part of our commitment to leveraging technology to enhance public safety and ensure that all members of our community have access to emergency assistance when they need it most.</p>
    <p style="color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.8;">Whether you're deaf, hard of hearing, have a speech disability, or find yourself in a scenario where speaking could put you in danger, Text-to-911 ensures you can still reach emergency services.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-5 p-4" style="background: #f8f5f0; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 4px solid #1c7f3f;">
  Please remember, voice calls to 911 are still the fastest and most efficient way to reach emergency services. Text-to-911 should only be used in emergency situations when calling is not an option.
</div>

<div class="mb-5 p-4" style="background: #f8f5f0; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 4px solid #C99C37;">
  <ul style="color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
<li class="mb-2">General Public</li>
<li class="mb-2">Deaf, hard of hearing, or individuals with speech disabilities</li>
<li class="mb-2">Domestic violence advocates</li>
<li class="mb-2">Individuals unable to speak due to medical or other conditions</li>
</ul>
<ul style="color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
<li class="mb-2">Calling 911 provides enhanced location information that may be limited when texting 911</li>
<li class="mb-2">Communication over text message is only available in English at this time</li>
<li class="mb-2">Photo and video sharing over text is not available. Some 911 Centers may message you separately to share multimedia</li>
<li class="mb-2">Wireless phone carriers have set a 160-character count limitation for texts</li>
</ul>
</div>



    


    

